@page "/uploadhelp"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Upload Help</PageTitle>

<div class="container-fluid upload-help-page">

    <div class="text-center mb-4">
        <h2><i class="fas fa-cloud-arrow-up me-2"></i>Upload Your Music</h2>
        <p class="lead">Get your tracks on StreamTunes in just a few steps. Let's walk through it!</p>
    </div>

    @* ───── Step 1 ───── *@
    <div class="help-section mb-4">
        <h4><span class="step-badge">1</span> Drop Your Files</h4>
        <p>
            Head over to the <a href="/upload-files">Upload Music</a> page, then drag &amp; drop your files onto the upload area — or click it to browse.
            We support <strong>MP3, WAV, FLAC, OGG, M4A, AAC,</strong> and <strong>WMA</strong> for audio,
            and <strong>JPEG</strong> and <strong>PNG</strong> for cover art.
        </p>
        <p>
            <i class="fas fa-circle-info text-primary me-1"></i>
            <strong>Important:</strong> Drop your audio files and cover art images <strong>together in the same upload</strong>.
            The app will automatically separate them and try to pair each image with the right audio file.
        </p>

        <div class="alert alert-info">
            <strong>Filenames:</strong> Name your files however you like &mdash; apostrophes, ampersands, extra dots,
            any language. Only the extension has to be one of the supported formats listed above. StreamTunes stores
            your files under its own internal names, so nothing about your filename reaches the website.
        </div>
        <p>
            Each song title is filled in from its filename (with underscores turned into spaces) and shown to you
            for review before anything is uploaded. Edit any title there, or later on Manage My Songs.
            Titles are limited to 200 characters and every song needs one.
        </p>
        <p>
            StreamTunes rejects the entire selection if any byte count or media format is invalid.
            Audio must fully decode with a positive duration, and JPEG/PNG cover art must decode successfully.
            After a successful upload, the exact original audio and cover art you supplied are retained privately
            alongside the playback MP3.
        </p>

        <h5 class="mt-3 mb-2"><i class="fas fa-wand-magic-sparkles me-1"></i> How Smart Matching Works</h5>
        <p>The upload process uses a multi-step approach to pair your cover art with the correct audio file:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>
                <strong>Filename similarity</strong> — The app compares filenames intelligently.
                Differences in spacing, hyphens, underscores, and casing can be handled automatically.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Image text extraction</strong> — If filename matching doesn't find a pair,
                the app reads any visible text in the image (such as a song title on album art) and
                uses that to find the right audio file.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>No match?</strong> — If neither method finds a match, the image is skipped
                and the song will use a default animated visual instead. You can always upload cover art
                later from the <a href="/creator/songs"><i class="fas fa-file-audio me-1"></i>Manage My Songs</a> page.
            </li>
        </ol>

        <h5 class="mt-3 mb-2"><i class="fas fa-check-circle text-success me-1"></i> Examples</h5>
        <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-sm help-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Audio File</th>
                        <th>Cover Art File</th>
                        <th>Result</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>Lipstick and Leather.mp3</code></td>
                        <td><code>Lipstick and Leather.jpeg</code></td>
                        <td><span class="badge bg-success">Paired <i class="fas fa-link ms-1"></i></span></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>Lipstick and Leather.mp3</code></td>
                        <td><code>Lipstick-and-Leather.jpeg</code></td>
                        <td><span class="badge bg-success">Paired <i class="fas fa-link ms-1"></i></span></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>Midnight Drive.wav</code></td>
                        <td><code>Midnight Drive.png</code></td>
                        <td><span class="badge bg-success">Paired <i class="fas fa-link ms-1"></i></span></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>Summer Vibes.flac</code></td>
                        <td><em class="text-muted">— image with "Summer Vibes" text on it —</em></td>
                        <td><span class="badge bg-success">Paired via text extraction <i class="fas fa-link ms-1"></i></span></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>Summer Vibes.flac</code></td>
                        <td><em class="text-muted">— none —</em></td>
                        <td><span class="badge bg-secondary">Default animation</span></td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        <h5 class="mt-3 mb-2"><i class="fas fa-crop-simple me-1"></i> Cover Art Tips</h5>
        <p>
            For best results, use a <strong>square</strong> image (e.g. 500 × 500 or 1000 × 1000 pixels).
            Rectangular images will still work — you can crop them to a perfect square later using the built-in crop tool on the
            <a href="/creator/songs"><i class="fas fa-file-audio me-1"></i>Manage My Songs</a> page. You have to upload at least 
            one song with cover art to see the tool.
        </p>

        <h5 class="mt-3 mb-2"><i class="fas fa-image me-1"></i> No Cover Art? No Problem!</h5>
        <p>
            If you skip the cover art during upload, your song will display this animated visual instead:
        </p>
        <div class="d-flex justify-content-center my-3">
            <div class="default-animation-preview">
                <dotlottie-wc src="https://lottie.host/07d61f77-2c9f-49a7-9884-4030d670f9ed/hSfkTa6ydt.lottie" class="preview-lottie-animation" autoplay loop></dotlottie-wc>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p>
            Looks pretty cool, right? But if you'd rather show off your own artwork, you can always upload a cover image later from the
            <a href="/creator/songs"><i class="fas fa-file-audio me-1"></i>Manage My Songs</a> page — no need to re-upload the song.
        </p>
    </div>

    @* ───── Step 2 ───── *@
    <div class="help-section mb-4">
        <h4><span class="step-badge">2</span> Song Titles &amp; Renaming</h4>
        <p>
            The filename becomes the song title automatically.
            For example, uploading <code>Lipstick and Leather.mp3</code> creates a song called <strong>Lipstick and Leather</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
            Changed your mind about the title? No problem — you can rename it anytime on the
            <a href="/creator/songs"><i class="fas fa-file-audio me-1"></i>Manage My Songs</a> page. Changing the display
            title does not rename the stored blobs.
        </p>
    </div>

    @* ───── Step 3 ───── *@
    <div class="help-section mb-4">
        <h4><span class="step-badge">3</span> Supported Formats at a Glance</h4>
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-6 mb-2">
                <div class="format-card">
                    <h6><i class="fas fa-music me-1"></i> Audio</h6>
                    <span class="badge bg-primary me-1">MP3</span>
                    <span class="badge bg-primary me-1">WAV</span>
                    <span class="badge bg-primary me-1">FLAC</span>
                    <span class="badge bg-primary me-1">OGG</span>
                    <span class="badge bg-primary me-1">M4A</span>
                    <span class="badge bg-primary me-1">AAC</span>
                    <span class="badge bg-primary">WMA</span>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 mb-2">
                <div class="format-card">
                    <h6><i class="fas fa-image me-1"></i> Cover Art</h6>
                    <span class="badge bg-info me-1">JPEG / JPG</span>
                    <span class="badge bg-info">PNG</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-4 mb-3">
        <a href="/upload-files" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
            <i class="fas fa-cloud-arrow-up me-2"></i>Start Uploading
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<style>
    .upload-help-page .lead {
        opacity: 0.85;
    }

    .step-badge {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        width: 28px;
        height: 28px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background-color: var(--bs-primary, #0d6efd);
        color: #fff;
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        margin-right: 8px;
    }

    .help-section {
        border-left: 3px solid var(--bs-primary, #0d6efd);
        padding-left: 16px;
    }

    .help-table {
        max-width: 720px;
    }

    .format-card {
        border: 1px solid rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.25);
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 12px 16px;
    }

    .default-animation-preview {
        width: 180px;
        height: 180px;
        border-radius: 8px;
        overflow: hidden;
        border: 2px solid #06acfc;
    }

    .preview-lottie-animation {
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
    }
</style>
